<title>USA: Chester Valley Bancorp Q1 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Chester Valley Bancorp Q1 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNINGTOWN, Pa. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>CHESTER VALLEY BANCORP INC. AND SUBSIDIARY</p>
<p>	   (Dollars in Thousands, Except for Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>			     Three Months Ended    September 30,</p>
<p>							1996	     1995</p>
<p> Total interest income			$5,379	   $5,043</p>
<p> Total interest expense			2,745	    2,701</p>
<p> Net interest income			   2,634	    2,342</p>
<p>Net interest income after provision</p>
<p>  for possible loan losses		   2,538	    2,250</p>
<p> Total other income				369		333</p>
<p> SAIF special assessment		     1,387		---</p>
<p> Other operating expenses		    1,817	    1,602</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			     (201)		596</p>
<p>Earnings per common share (A):</p>
<p>  Primary					 (0.12)	     0.36</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
<p>NOTE: The company reported net income of $631,000 before the SAIF assessment. (A)  Per share amounts have been restated to reflect the effect of the 5% stock dividend paid in September 1996.</p>
